From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:00:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(v1): optimize prefix retention, multimodal hashing, and
 request IPC

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
with candidate-55's series applied through 0810.

Rationale: Reduces CPU frontend overhead across long-context and multi-turn
workloads via Int32TokenIds zero-copy PickleBuffer request IPC, lazy PIL image
metadata caching with parallel blake3 hashing and prefix-cache stripping, and
hybrid prefix-cache block-boundary retention in KVCacheCoordinator and Scheduler
(maintaining >=98.5% multi-turn hit rate under eviction pressure).

Quality implications: None; deterministic prefix-cache retention, IPC round-trips,
and lazy multimodal fallback are verified across 64K-100K stress tests.

Tests: pytest -q -p deepseek_models tests/multimodal/test_prefix_cache_fastpath.py
tests/v1/core/test_new_request_data_ipc.py
tests/v1/core/test_prefix_cache_retention_probe.py.

Upstream status: local candidate-60 patch
